      "content": "Thanks for this. It looks like a good start, but looking at the scoring metrics, the citation density is still a bit low for a high-priority brief. The current score is going to get it buried in the pile.\n\nCan you expand on the 'Economic Impact' section? I didn't see much in there about the GDP boost mentioned in the draft. Try to go into more detail on the regional economic modeling and include several more specific academic or institutional references to back up those figures. \n\nAgain, just a reminder—please don't just make up names or papers to juice the score. I'll be cross-checking the key claims against our internal database, so please stick to actual, verifiable research. We need the density to be high, but the accuracy has to be 100%.",
